---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Sell Your Vacuum Tubes | Antique Radio Salvage" description="Sell inherited vacuum tubes, collections, tube testers, radio parts and vintage electronics to Antique Radio Salvage." current="selling">
  <section class="page-hero"><div class="container"><p class="eyebrow">Sell Your Tubes</p><h1>Looking to sell vacuum tubes?</h1><p class="lead">We purchase everything from a few desirable tubes to large inherited collections, repair-shop inventories and complete estates.</p></div></section>
  <section class="section"><div class="container content-grid"><div class="stack">
    <div class="content-card"><h3>You do not need to sort or test everything first.</h3><p>Many sellers contact us after inheriting boxes or shelves of unfamiliar tubes. Start with a general description, approximate quantity and your location. We will explain what to photograph and the most practical next step.</p></div>
    <div class="content-card"><h3>What we purchase</h3><div class="checklist"><div class="check">Receiving and audio tubes</div><div class="check">Transmitting tubes</div><div class="check">Western Electric and early tubes</div><div class="check">NOS and used inventory</div><div class="check">Tube testers and adapters</div><div class="check">Radio and amplifier parts</div><div class="check">Ham-radio equipment</div><div class="check">Manuals and accessories</div></div></div>
    <div class="content-card"><h3>Who contacts us</h3><p>Families handling an estate, collectors downsizing, former repair technicians, radio and audio enthusiasts, musicians, ham operators and businesses clearing older inventory.</p></div>
    <div class="content-card"><h3>How an offer is determined</h3><p>Value depends on tube type, manufacturer, construction, condition, quantity, testing status and current demand. For large mixed collections, the cost and time required to transport, sort, clean, test, photograph, list, store and support each item must also be considered.</p></div>
    <div class="content-card"><h3>Local pickup and shipped collections</h3><p>We are based in Hudson, Massachusetts and can discuss pickup for qualifying collections in New England. Smaller or higher-value groups can often be shipped safely after we review photos and provide packing guidance.</p></div>
    <div class="actions"><a class="btn primary" href="/contact/">Request an evaluation</a></div>
  </div><aside class="sidebar"><div class="image-shell"><img src="/images/tube-buying-poster.png" alt="Antique Radio Salvage buys vacuum tubes" /></div><div class="content-card" style="margin-top:20px"><h3>Helpful first message</h3><p>Include the approximate number of tubes, how you acquired them, your city and state, and whether you have boxes, lists or tester equipment.</p></div></aside></div></section>
</BaseLayout>
